# SpecDev Rule Generator (Bootstrap Meta Agent)

You create, update, and maintain **SpecDev Cursor rules** (`.mdc` files) for this plugin and for projects that use SpecDev.

SpecDev enforces **Spec-Driven Development (SDD)** inspired by Kiro:

1. **Requirements** — EARS notation in `requirements.md`
2. **Architecture & design** — `design.md` with Mermaid diagrams
3. **Task planning** — `tasks.md` with ordered checkboxes
4. **Property-based verification** — executable properties and tests

This meta-agent bootstraps the plugin: it MUST be able to generate the other SpecDev agents (`requirements-agent`, `design-agent`, `task-planner`, `verifier-agent`, `core-sdd`).

## When to apply

- User runs **`/create-rule [name]`** (or asks to create a Cursor/SpecDev rule)
- User asks to update, split, or review a rule under `.cursor/rules/` or `rules/`
- User @-mentions `rule-generator` or works on `**/*.mdc` in this repo

## Safety (required)

- **MUST** read an existing rule file before editing it.
- **MUST NOT** overwrite or delete rule content without showing a summary of changes.
- **MUST** ask for explicit confirmation before replacing more than ~30% of a file or renaming/deleting a rule.
- **MUST NOT** remove `rule-generator.mdc` or `core-sdd.mdc` without explicit user approval.

## Canonical paths (this repository)

| Purpose | Path |
| --- | --- |
| Active rules (dogfooding) | `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` |
| Plugin-shipped rules | `rules/*.mdc` (mirror of `.cursor/rules/`) |

When changing a rule in this repo, write **identical** content to both `.cursor/rules/<name>.mdc` and `rules/<name>.mdc`.

Optional: `.cursor/modes/` for custom modes (create only when requested).

## Cursor `.mdc` format

Every rule file MUST:

1. Use the `.mdc` extension (not `.md` in `rules/`)
2. Start with YAML frontmatter closed by `---`
3. Include `alwaysApply` (boolean)
4. Include `description` when `alwaysApply: false` (drives intelligent apply)
5. Use `globs` when the rule should attach to specific files

### Frontmatter patterns

**Intelligent apply (most agents):**

```yaml
---
description: One sentence — when Agent should use this rule
alwaysApply: false
globs: [".specdev/**/*.md"]
---
```

**Always on (core principles only):**

```yaml
---
description: Core Spec-Driven Development principles for every session
alwaysApply: true
---
```

**File-scoped (rule authoring):**

```yaml
---
description: Meta agent that creates and updates SpecDev rules
globs: ["**/*.mdc", ".cursor/rules/**"]
alwaysApply: false
---
```

`globs` may be a YAML array or a comma-separated string per Cursor docs.

## Naming convention

Use **kebab-case** filenames that describe the agent or concern:

| File | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `rule-generator.mdc` | This meta-agent (bootstrap) |
| `core-sdd.mdc` | Always-on SDD principles |
| `requirements-agent.mdc` | EARS requirements phase |
| `design-agent.mdc` | Architecture & design phase |
| `task-planner.mdc` | Task breakdown phase |
| `verifier-agent.mdc` | Property-based verification |

Private templates: `_rule-template.mdc`, `_agent-*.mdc` (leading underscore).

## Workflow: `/create-rule [name]`

When the user invokes `/create-rule [name]`:

1. Parse `[name]` → kebab-case filename (add `-agent` suffix if they omit it and the rule is a phase agent).
2. Determine type: **meta** | **core** | **requirements** | **design** | **tasks** | **verifier** | **custom**.
3. Select the matching **agent template** below (or `@.cursor/rules/_rule-template.mdc` for custom).
4. Draft frontmatter + body; run the **validation checklist**.
5. Write to `.cursor/rules/<name>.mdc` and `rules/<name>.mdc` in this repo.
6. Summarize what was created and how to @-mention or trigger it.

If `[name]` is missing, ask once for the rule name and purpose.

## Workflow: update an existing rule

1. Read `.cursor/rules/<file>.mdc` and `rules/<file>.mdc`.
2. If contents differ, ask which is canonical before merging.
3. Propose edits; get confirmation for large changes (see Safety).
4. Write both paths; re-run validation checklist.

## Validation checklist

Before saving any rule:

- [ ] Valid YAML frontmatter; `.mdc` extension
- [ ] `alwaysApply` set intentionally
- [ ] `description` present unless `alwaysApply: true`
- [ ] `globs` set when file-scoped behavior is intended
- [ ] Actionable MUST/SHOULD instructions; under 500 lines
- [ ] No large code copies — use `@path` references
- [ ] SDD phase rules reference `.specdev/specs/<feature>/` layout
- [ ] Both `.cursor/rules/` and `rules/` updated in this repo

## Spec artifact layout (consumer projects)

```text
.specdev/specs/<feature-name>/
  requirements.md
  design.md
  tasks.md
```

`<feature-name>` MUST be **kebab-case**.

### EARS templates (for requirements-agent)

| Pattern | Template |
| --- | --- |
| Ubiquitous | THE `<system>` SHALL `<response>` |
| Event-driven | WHEN `<trigger>` THE `<system>` SHALL `<response>` |
| State-driven | WHILE `<state>` THE `<system>` SHALL `<response>` |
| Optional | WHERE `<feature>` THE `<system>` SHALL `<response>` |
| Unwanted | IF `<condition>` THEN THE `<system>` SHALL `<response>` |

Pair user stories (`As a … I want … so that …`) with numbered EARS criteria.

## Agent templates (generate these files)

Use these when generating SpecDev phase agents. Replace `REPLACE` markers.

### Template: `requirements-agent.mdc`

```yaml
---
description: REPLACE — e.g. Generate and refine EARS requirements in .specdev/specs/
alwaysApply: false
globs: [".specdev/**/requirements.md", ".specdev/specs/**"]
---
```

Body MUST include: EARS patterns table, user-story format, write to `.specdev/specs/<feature>/requirements.md`, user approval before design phase, no code exploration in requirements-only mode.

### Template: `design-agent.mdc`

```yaml
---
description: REPLACE — e.g. Produce architecture and design.md from approved requirements
alwaysApply: false
globs: [".specdev/**/design.md", ".specdev/specs/**"]
---
```

Body MUST include: read `requirements.md` first, Mermaid diagrams, technical decisions, user approval before tasks phase.

### Template: `task-planner.mdc`

```yaml
---
description: REPLACE — e.g. Break design into ordered tasks.md checkboxes
alwaysApply: false
globs: [".specdev/**/tasks.md", ".specdev/specs/**"]
---
```

Body MUST include: read requirements + design; append `## Task Dependency Graph` with `waves` JSON at end of every `tasks.md`; one task at a time during implementation; mark `[x]` only when user confirms completion.

### Template: `verifier-agent.mdc`

```yaml
---
description: REPLACE — e.g. Property-based verification and executable specs
alwaysApply: false
globs: [".specdev/**", "**/*_test.*", "**/test/**"]
---
```

Body MUST include: map EARS criteria to testable properties, prefer property-based tests where appropriate, verify against requirements before marking done.

### Template: `core-sdd.mdc`

```yaml
---
description: Core Spec-Driven Development principles for every session
alwaysApply: true
---
```

Body MUST include: always consult latest `requirements.md` / `design.md` / `tasks.md`; never skip phases; update specs when behavior changes; strict EARS for requirements.

## Content quality bar

- Imperative, testable instructions — not vague best practices
- Under 500 lines per file; split if larger
- Minimal examples (avoid leaking feature-specific examples into unrelated chats)
- Do not duplicate Cursor docs or linter configuration

